# Phase 16 follow-up: this repo had no .gitattributes, so a Windows checkout
# (Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true) got CRLF line endings
# while a Linux/macOS checkout got LF -- same git blobs, different bytes on
# disk depending on which machine built dist/playables/. Harmless (nowhere
# near any Stability §1-3 size limit either way), but the certification
# bundle should be byte-identical regardless of which machine builds it, not
# "usually fine, off by a few KB sometimes." This forces LF on checkout for
# every text source file, on every platform, regardless of the user's own
# core.autocrlf setting -- and marks the two binary asset types explicitly
# so git never guesses wrong on those.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.js  text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf

*.woff2 binary
*.png binary
